{
  "description": "Preserve Self-EvolveRec’s diagnostic interface while adapting its probes to the corrected BERT4Rec backbone. DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) returns measured metrics and metric_definitions; diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis) explains those results using their definitions.",
  "motivation": "Make model diagnosis useful for architecture refinement without assuming unavailable review data or simulator traits. Compare changes using macro-average validation HR@10 across all four datasets.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve the host ModelView interfaces and inspect the actual trained view.model. Support batches shaped B × L containing (None, sequence, positive, negative). Respect left padding, reserved mask tokens, masked-target training and appended-mask inference; never expose the prediction target through bidirectional input. Use only observed histories, titles, descriptions and timestamps. Treat diversity/conformity traits as unobserved. Maintain one independently trained checkpoint per category and keep the embedded predictor consistent with its architecture. The simulator receives full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty training users, five per category.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe(view, device):\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        set view.model to evaluation mode\n        disable gradients\n        for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n            apply BERT4Rec-compatible masking and padding rules\n            compute supported diagnostic measurements through ModelView\n            aggregate measurements with explicit valid counts\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics: aggregated measurements,\n                metric_definitions: definitions and availability limits}\n\nfunction diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    include measured metrics and their definitions\n    identify unavailable evidence explicitly\n    request evidence-grounded interpretations and testable hypotheses\n    prohibit invented attributes and independent-model fusion",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Connects a stable diagnostic interface to family-specific model behavior and explicit evidence limits.",
    "negative": "Primarily an adaptation contract; it does not specify a new diagnostic algorithm."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support reproducible diagnosis-driven refinement across sequential architectures.",
    "negative": "Value depends on choosing reliable probes and demonstrating validation improvements; no results are supplied."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 6,
    "positive": "The fixed interfaces and batch structure make the integration scope clear.",
    "negative": "Correct masking, left-padding handling, metric aggregation and checkpoint–predictor consistency require careful implementation."
  }
}
